  The reel_script says the supervisor Babu was arrested by police on Saturday, which matches the article, but the draft says the 658 g of gold and Rs.75 lakh value were stolen; the article says the jewels 'மாயமாகியது' (went missing), not explicitly theft by a named thief — minor, but the reel_script also states 'பாபுவுக்கு இந்தத் திருட்டில் தொடர்பு' which is fine.
  The slides_spec 'hl2' and slide text state 'பாபுவிடம் இருந்து 550 கிராம் நகை பறிமுதல்' correctly, but the slide 'தேடப்படுவோர்' line 1 has an unclosed <b> tag ('<b>2' with no closing tag), a malformed Tamil/HTML fragment.
  The slides_spec 'hl1' headline says 'ஒருவர்' (one person) while the article indicates two others are wanted; the headline omits the arrest count inconsistency only partially, and the 'யார் கைது?' slide line 'சனிக்கிழமை போலீசார் கைது செய்தனர்' repeats the arrest without a new fact, which is not an error but duplicates.
  The caption includes 'ஸ்மித்தேஸ் என்பவருக்குச் சொந்தமான நகைப்பட்டறை' (shop owned by Smithes) — this is in the article, so acceptable.
  The reel_script omits that the owner is Smithes, which is not required, but it does mention the arrested person's age and role correctly.
